      },
      "lineNbr": 2361,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T12:21:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: Is this intentional (the same for unamp host path) ? Throughout this operation we don\u0027t update the IOMMUs pagetables even though we modify the mappings in the host stage-2. In this window, a DMA capable hardware can issue transactions targeting this (unmapped from AP) region.\n\nAlso do we need to map this back explicitly ? We can leave it un-mapped and it will fault on the first access.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2361,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 2361,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "2c6cbc9eaa1f61e15c3dd9076c5f3ed3f0663fa4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3e681db_70ad1fee",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2361,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T09:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a such device does this, the memory would be protected anyway by TZPC. So no security issue here so I believe no need to waste time on updating the iommu.\n\nIt is mapped to make sure we re-install a block mapping where possible. I don\u0027t believe we treat this as a hot-path so spending a bit more time to get a more optimal stage-2 is probably a good tradeoff .",
      "parentUuid": "0a04db3f_040bddc3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2361,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 2361,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "2c6cbc9eaa1f61e15c3dd9076c5f3ed3f0663fa4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ae451e2_f1c0ecd3",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2361,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-31T15:32:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We probably/hopefully won\u0027t get speculative accesses from DMA either, so I think it\u0027s fine to leave the memory mapped in the IOMMU.\n\nHowever, I agree with Seb that eagerly remapping seems unnecessary. We\u0027ll remap the range on a faulting host access, and I _think_ we trigger coalescing on that path.",
      "parentUuid": "c3e681db_70ad1fee",
